        "container": null,
        "content": [
          {
            "citations": null,
            "text": "Here are two key aspects of gravity:\n\n1. **Universal Attraction**: Gravity is a fundamental force that causes all objects with mass to attract each other. The strength of this attraction depends on the masses of the objects and the distance between them.\n\n2. **Weight and Acceleration**: Gravity gives objects weight and causes them to accelerate when falling. On Earth, this acceleration is approximately 9.8 m/s², meaning falling objects increase their speed by about 9.8 meters per second every second (in the absence of air resistance).",
